}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ad59df0a-7322-c143-934f-233fbe2f7a69"],

Cell["\<\
A Hypergraph draws itself by default, the way a Graph does, so HypergraphPlot \
is needed only in order to pass options.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d59d3b79-9934-c74f-aa4c-06a541074edc"],

Cell["Arrays", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"bebf4c42-a484-204f-89ac-07a732cd38b1"],

Cell["\<\
An array is a nesting of lists, and one object holds any of them: nothing \
about the structure of an array depends on what sits in its entries, which \
may be numbers, elements of a finite field, symbolic expressions or labels. \
The order of an array is its number of indices, and an array of order n is an \
n-array: a vector is a 1-array and a matrix is a 2-array. A scalar is the \
0-array. An array is regular when all of its indices range over the same \
length, and only a regular array can carry an index symmetry.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d7e1ea5d-dcdf-544e-8881-bb6a5cb46aa7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "What an array is made of is read off its entries by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayDomain", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "38e6b3cc-0c02-e341-8470-2232ffbc646a"],
 " rather than declared alongside them. The symmetry is the one thing it is \
told rather than asked, being a claim about the entries that they may or may \
not bear out."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7426bcd2-c878-0c43-809d-29b10a4d6e6e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayObject", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "e126fc14-1d60-a04e-b928-e1583a8b62a1"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "an array, whatever its entries are"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c34e3ee5-f544-1641-8cd9-8c48a2b8797b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["GenerateSymbolicArray", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"a1f821d0-2c53-1049-8869-7f55322d40b3"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "build one whose entries are a name applied to the indices"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0b212b1e-3c47-5c45-a51e-4fa1b6c2791f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayOrder", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "df1d4f9d-f8df-6c48-b984-1598fc3e2f6b"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the number of indices"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e3f69c40-5331-9944-9b6c-e2088f2bb3ca"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayDimensions", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "295fbfc3-f73f-4648-8058-b5a2de646446"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the lengths of the indices"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2ae12c1f-3508-4b4f-a66a-db3da52a0de2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArraySymmetry", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "3ad305a4-5d98-ba48-8201-6ea6529012e1"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the index symmetry: \"Rigid\", \"Cyclic\" or \"Symmetric\""
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9b76713f-52dc-8e43-981e-cda5d886de7b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayDomain", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "52717b8a-459c-9849-9d1c-6e2aa403d57c"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the value domain of the entries, or \"Expression\""
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7d4b4c53-6c91-be41-bcca-9419df590ae0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayEntries", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "5fba5721-6945-bd40-9a23-e3630cc0b922"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the entries, as a nested list"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"01b2571e-2bb7-9940-9537-b7fc051da7c1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["RegularArrayQ", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "40331787-8386-e847-ac89-71841a3ae4f0"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "whether every index ranges over the same length"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e2ef1549-93c9-1243-bbf8-c081f1b6ec47"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayObjectQ", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "0518509d-4950-4048-910a-44cea5d9fadb"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "test for a valid array object"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c6e2df9b-fa94-444b-9d81-a8c45be62571"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Dimensions and Normal work directly on an array object, and further \
properties are read as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"arr", "[", "\"\<prop\>\"", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"bb2d2fd9-0422-434a-acdb-3132068df6fc"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e186e6dc-3eb0-2a4f-b703-0a4d8e9a4f35"],

Cell["Special arrays", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"02387c2a-99ef-f14b-a0bb-59a9b12e55f6"],

Cell["\<\
Constant arrays and the generalized Kronecker deltas, in any order, dimension \
and value domain. Each declares the strongest symmetry that actually holds of \
it.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"75fdf1c8-fdbb-d94b-93e9-631143438797"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ZeroArray", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "b75df06a-6b28-d640-b0f8-af6dab265a33"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "every entry zero"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d7abfac9-8e56-c14e-9840-5ad96793f651"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["OneArray", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "cf89236d-2b34-984c-9ce1-e4d3108dde52"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "every entry one"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"75f817a8-4291-0440-b357-25b739720064"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["IdentityArray", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "6a23c540-ef61-2544-a63d-b2b0ce1d1b4c"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "one where all the indices agree, zero elsewhere"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"595de4fe-9ee5-f444-9bd6-820338065371"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["PartialIdentityArray", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"fe037ff7-71d7-6c49-9522-e306605a239f"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "one where the indices at chosen positions agree"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"dae75c24-e20b-ca49-94a0-8d21f0cb8013"],

Cell["Contraction", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"326f4f0f-faf0-4a48-99b0-8a49bf55bea3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayMultiply", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "5a3bb5f9-b7e6-f844-8aa7-ee773c4e3c00"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "contract arrays by an index specification, in the manner of Einstein \
summation"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9c385ccc-aaeb-fb49-bd1c-6b7bd906bccc"],

Cell["\<\
The specification is written either as a string, \"ij,jk->ik\", or as a rule \
between lists of index labels. An index may occur in any number of the arrays \
and in the output as well, so diagonals and three-way contractions are \
expressible, not only pairwise ones. A 0-array is named by an empty group of \
labels, and contracting every index away gives one back.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0c487193-45bb-f44d-8b6c-6657f57d4dca"],

Cell["Drawing arrays", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"90d9745e-e740-324c-80ce-0a4153e3cc81"],

Cell["\<\
There are two families, and an array of any order may be drawn in either. The \
flat family gives plane pictures throughout: a row of cells at order one, a \
grid at order two, and above that a nesting of those, a grid whose cells hold \
grids. The spatial family gives cubes arranged in space throughout: a line of \
cubes, a plane of them, a lattice, and above that the same lattices tiled \
through space, block beside block, all in one picture.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7d80c71c-4938-ef49-bd8b-0b21df0f7662"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Which indices go outside and which inside is a choice rather than a fact \
about the array, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\"\<Nesting\>\"", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "d3a35a3c-d9f6-c94d-8f9c-bd82f620f6e5"],
 " makes it. A flat picture holds one or two indices at a time and a spatial \
one holds three, so that is the only difference between the two defaults."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4774c9f8-15a3-2642-bb68-5e88d7c83d56"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayGraphics", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "cc6b36a1-16c9-f442-a31e-30e184ba95c5"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "draw an array of any order in the plane"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"195cca9c-8c73-2143-bd98-1d44a670d00a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayGraphics3D", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "96ffea02-5a6d-8146-bd63-1a62c8a845db"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "draw an array of any order as cubes in space"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"72ecf788-38bc-c648-bcc9-ea087b2e35fa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayNesting", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "a2e04dc5-4e89-f549-883b-93d8407f24b6"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "how the indices are split by default, for either family"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"aae4e1f6-e48d-bb43-8b7a-67b3e328000d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypermatrixGraphics", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"2deef6c0-d42c-9347-8499-6ede510e6709"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "draw every array of a hypermatrix, in the plane"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f3aba039-9a01-1f4e-8b8d-bbd0f0c07d8e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypermatrixGraphics3D", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"6b3f788d-1b9d-5a4d-93fa-ba71f8560a32"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the same, as cubes in space"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"27a3e11a-35ff-3c4e-bb8d-0c45beb5611a"],

Cell["Adding and multiplying entry by entry", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0b98945a-c6fe-264a-9ded-2200bf91e321"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayAdd", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "cff43379-58bc-1846-b4ea-79a7919b63a6"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "add arrays entry by entry"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"860c05b1-7118-3b41-adc9-655e6d2f23a4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayTimes", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "e3b5233a-c78f-3647-9136-c395c2a7ade2"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "multiply arrays entry by entry"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e8059c1c-7a3b-2041-a3fa-305630371b5b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "These are the multilinear structure of arrays, as against the contraction \
ArrayMultiply. Arrays of the same dimensions combine entry by entry, and a \
0-array, having no shape of its own, reaches every entry \[LongDash] which is \
why scalar multiplication needs no name of its own. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Plus", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "e143b568-9d32-7348-bdb3-7eabce51df60"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Times", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "34cccb09-a7c7-b843-9396-631b3f711985"],
 " on array objects are the same operations, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"2", " ", "a"}], " ", "+", " ", "b"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"0ad65e80-c043-454b-8532-e87fd79a3ebd"],
 " means what it looks like."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f4010aa9-04b2-7b4f-9715-8c0e33e92f74"],

Cell["Equational identities", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b61792be-81ce-4d4d-a071-079b177eb879"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["FindArrayEquations", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"149e044b-72bb-c846-b8f5-4d862b2d0121"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "search for equations between all nestings of given operations over given \
arguments"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8fb4403d-1864-054e-b0a8-fb3eeebd97df"],

Cell["\<\
The search screens candidates on random numerical arrays first, which is \
fast, and verifies only the survivors on symbolic arrays. Matrix \
multiplication on three arguments returns associativity; the Fish product on \
five returns a twisted ternary associativity; the Bhattacharya-Mesner product \
on five returns nothing. An operation of arity one may be nested, so that the \
involutivity of a transpose is within reach, and an equation that follows \
from the others is not reported.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2908c275-e931-6c44-a6dc-5602d1068d0c"],

Cell["From hypergraphs to hypermatrices", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"db5511fd-576f-0c47-bea8-5bdfaa6242da"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two halves of the package meet here. An edge has an arity and a \
symmetry type; an array has an order and a symmetry; and the two vocabularies \
line up one for one \[LongDash] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\"\<Directed\>\"", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "db4387ae-c4d2-2744-a43c-27c57edaa72b"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\"\<Rigid\>\"", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "7d110168-cee4-3a41-953b-495635c6139d"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\"\<Cyclic\>\"", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "350cf2bc-8aea-624a-a604-52a8ac3166e4"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\"\<Cyclic\>\"", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "e5ac96be-ad75-9a4e-9d04-a36bbdf978d4"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\"\<Unordered\>\"", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"bf72a95d-b73b-e14d-864f-f7ee4434acac"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\"\<Symmetric\>\"", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"7b154237-0118-634a-9ff0-9de9700fc635"],
 ". An array holds one symmetry and one order, so the edges are gathered by \
arity and symmetry type together and each group becomes one array."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2c404ce5-b25e-d642-911d-2e982d227580"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["AdjacencyHypermatrix", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"7bccc0a3-a77d-494b-8c70-f6c9557030dc"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the adjacency hypermatrix of a hypergraph"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b95ef2f9-dd19-8141-9c90-3f53f724da73"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Identical copies of an edge share an entry, so a repeated edge comes out as \
an integer multiple. With ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Labeled\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"2560bff0-f300-c548-b1c8-ef63e289ef03"],
 " the entries are the edge labels themselves rather than counts, which needs \
the hypergraph to be simple \[LongDash] one entry cannot hold two labels."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"41a85886-04bf-fe49-a60f-daaa2ab1e5e0"],

Cell["\<\
The entry at an index tuple counts the edges sitting on it, and every tuple \
of an orbit reads the same count, which is what makes each array carry its \
symmetry by construction. Nothing is lost in the passage: the canonical \
entries name exactly the edges that went in.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cee305d7-98c7-fd49-869f-79b356d9c231"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The vertices are a set, so numbering the indices is a choice; the \
Hypergraph constructor makes it by storing its vertices sorted. That is \
deterministic but not invariant \[LongDash] renaming the vertices can permute \
the indices \[LongDash] so for an invariant of the isomorphism class, compose \
with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["CanonicalHypergraph", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"62ea48a3-0e0e-cf43-89b5-e36279a1fe17"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"13095ef9-3f2d-c940-9fe0-81505b1127ae"],

Cell["Hypermatrices", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"943bff84-7df2-364a-a3b1-9ed94d0bc9ad"],

Cell["\<\
A hypermatrix is a list of arrays held in canonical order: lowest order \
first, then the shorter dimensions, then symmetry taking symmetric before \
cyclic before rigid. Giving the same arrays in a different order produces the \
identical expression.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8ffe4f0e-7ba6-794b-b688-959a8950af4f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Hypermatrix", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ce71ddc5-661a-b848-abcc-eab61d3ca32e"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "a canonically ordered list of arrays"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"275cce6a-482e-2543-adf7-aeb2620a510b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypermatrixArrays", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"7ed72aef-3ffa-7b47-8cf5-cb6369a31b0e"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the arrays, in canonical order"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"05876add-847e-044c-9131-11af6257bc99"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypermatrixQ", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "c43548fe-beeb-2f4f-8620-c6c9a4241043"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "test for a valid hypermatrix object"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"da5f2029-e537-8f4a-9e5a-7241af869abd"],

Cell["Messages", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ec682e16-8f8e-5649-9290-f473bfad0575"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Edge", "::", "sym"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"fd8c8d9b-a59a-044d-8b45-c7a1d9af9335"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the given edge symmetry type is not one of the three recognized ones"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"168c5121-68b5-414a-9009-13b61d812397"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Edge", "::", "spec"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"db8fc07c-9018-fd4f-b1cc-69b584146a60"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the expression is not a valid hyperedge specification"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bd72e4d1-1b0f-6641-b7ca-081733a59cc3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Hypergraph", "::", "spec"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"1bc7d8ff-f51b-e449-8c00-0ca09ff17732"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the expression is not a valid hypergraph specification"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4493d770-667d-5d4d-9eaf-c3835bce509f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Hypergraph", "::", "vlbl"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"736012dd-4148-8246-ae2c-87f60288c1f4"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "one vertex identifier was given more than one label"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e1c5105f-b38b-b64f-8551-98dac8f544a1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"CanonicalHypergraph", "::", "large"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"340d2548-e9db-ad4b-8851-471db43a8061"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the isomorphism search will be slow at this size"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f62f6010-a46a-ab4c-aaa9-c19533b44831"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayObject", "::", "nosym"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"f17937b1-20c8-4a41-ba03-91b7809b1d9c"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the entries are not invariant under the declared symmetry"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1e97a0b9-e07a-e541-bb7d-c79a1a861004"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayObject", "::", "irreg"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"4a171333-3aa9-7c4a-94b3-ade78ecb479a"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "an irregular array cannot carry a symmetry"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e2935c75-fda8-0f40-b408-bab1df4818e0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayObject", "::", "data"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"b688254c-ffbd-7a4d-a03d-d49e98298be4"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the entries are not a rectangular array"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b3c4a487-e506-764f-8b51-c110d692a35c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"GenerateSymbolicArray", "::", "name"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"1d2e7e62-5ab8-a84f-bb6b-74838e175aea"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "an array name must be a symbol or a string"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ae0eb2bf-7a75-6d45-a7f9-cd39549227d8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Hypermatrix", "::", "arrays"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"7399eaa4-7d73-3945-9477-2b8ccc1cf9e4"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "something given was not an array"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"25e9cc34-e194-fe48-a5c2-a0b99642371c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayMultiply", "::", "rank"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"c3bddf6f-f045-e74c-908a-a30e178ede72"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "an array has a different number of indices from its specification"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"91e9dced-5d9e-8f47-a919-48658f77aa43"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayMultiply", "::", "dims"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"e58655ae-8be3-df43-8e6b-8a17b7b5bd8e"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "one index label is used with two different lengths"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b113436d-e035-b645-9cdf-cff936aaa3dd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayMultiply", "::", "out"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"ab30317b-1391-8e49-90e4-19ce2a639b4c"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "an output index does not occur among the inputs"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5b46e23c-6b06-e540-8fee-e7d5f0b80f77"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"FindArrayEquations", "::", "arity"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"f21fd670-11ec-da4f-b3bc-7d909a12feef"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the arity of an operation could not be determined"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"df743210-726f-574b-a8ef-e9bd9ba4c941"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"FindArrayEquations", "::", "eval"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"d4c8e084-14ce-404e-954c-bccc0986b62a"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "no nesting evaluated on arrays of the shape used"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2afc53c9-90c9-e74e-a7d7-8f275b2ac630"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"FindArrayEquations", "::", "shape"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"f468c0ff-42dd-454c-bcb4-2ff5a6b695fa"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "no order from 1 to 5 suits every operation"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8641d2d8-3a3f-1445-bd98-4e866e004ac4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"FindArrayEquations", "::", "depth"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"2c82caa3-8c9a-5d40-809f-bb5ddee1d1a1"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "\"UnaryDepth\" is not a non-negative integer"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2ffa4f7c-6a3e-4d4d-ba10-2e68ec0cbe50"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayAdd", "::", "dims"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"96a35872-a06c-cc4e-91e8-d3a4e5c59f02"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the arrays are not of the same dimensions"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9b6ab00f-4cf7-0a42-b9a7-c9ba84531cd3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayTimes", "::", "dims"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"aa2a602e-552d-0c40-bcbd-94218d5fbe2f"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the same, for multiplication entry by entry"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"467d53ae-183d-1849-a82a-f56d4046f9f1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayGraphics", "::", "nesting"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"e6345a34-b153-0544-9bfb-26379fe4f408"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the given nesting does not account for every index"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"293a4fd3-a617-024d-b573-646700215772"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayGraphics", "::", "block"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"299b4244-b75d-2e45-9e95-54165fe176ce"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "a block of more than two indices has no flat picture"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"15e00909-01ef-8e49-b8a6-76086c8a39c9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayGraphics3D", "::", "block"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"56334bc0-ea03-5848-ae21-07d6ee093918"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "a block of more than three indices has nowhere to go in space"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"722121e8-3d18-9443-8c99-9a94b955beb1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"AdjacencyHypermatrix", "::", "hg"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"7c24d752-1b9b-c844-8191-ae8f22d97d03"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the argument is not a hypergraph"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"20feaa46-9db9-8348-82f3-46c034e4eff0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"HypergraphRule", "::", "hg"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"46f85a01-0a7f-1443-af5b-952ac8370a9f"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "a side of a rule is not a hypergraph"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e89c7d75-3ab8-e748-814f-8ba35cf91be1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"HypergraphRuleApply", "::", "rule"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"fccc186d-e723-3c40-85e1-f84005bd6646"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "what was given is not a rewrite rule"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"dcb0a51e-f4da-3046-b29a-c081b7a2f6a1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"AdjacencyHypermatrix", "::", "nonsimple"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"219f2eee-7e04-924e-8eb0-13bec0985067"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "labels cannot be entries unless no edge is repeated"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9115f1cc-578d-b04e-8341-a435e11a0ff9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayGraphics", "::", "big"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"d2425662-675d-f64e-9a35-fe35e3a9e856"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the array has too many entries to be drawn legibly"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ea10e589-50f9-6e4b-9227-77c8ad95df61"],

Cell["Rewriting", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"8bca4450-d87a-d246-a270-c30ae0e7fc8e"],

Cell["\<\
A rewrite rule is a pair of hypergraphs. Applying it means finding the ways \
its input sits inside a hypergraph, and for each of them replacing what was \
matched by the output. Each such way is an event, reported as an association \
saying not only what the new hypergraph is but what was matched, what was \
created and what was destroyed.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"01a9cc04-d544-2f4d-b422-e4d3f72e12fe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphRule", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "e46802d7-39ca-7947-a48a-8560be26d4e1"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "a rewrite rule, as a pair of hypergraphs"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"24da2735-c29c-c04d-95af-78c11e0cc4e6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphRuleQ", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "84ad5209-09d0-454b-a2b3-a769ddae216f"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "test for a valid rule"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0582cab5-ce68-4d45-a08e-fadc725045f4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphRuleApply", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"30af3c74-e7e8-7645-9bc4-702df78e16e8"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "apply a rule, giving one event per match; rule[hg] is the same"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fc16efbe-9803-d542-8426-90e2f13a3144"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphRuleMatches", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"1bde2262-1e9c-454e-9e61-1b5c25d83dd4"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the ways the input sits inside a hypergraph, without rewriting"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a277b6f6-f663-3a4b-936e-9566a4762d83"],

Cell["\<\
Symmetry types must agree between a pattern edge and the edge it lies on, and \
the pattern is matched over the orderings that symmetry allows.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5eb5220b-1d9a-b045-90c6-e3df9daa81c3"],

Cell["\<\
A label on a rule's input is read three ways. A bare symbol is a variable: it \
matches whatever label it is laid against and remembers it, and the output's \
labels are expressions in those variables, written out with the bindings put \
in \[LongDash] which is how a pair of composable edges labelled x and y \
becomes one labelled for their composite. No label at all is a wildcard. \
Anything else is a literal. Vertex labels bind the same way as edge labels, \
so a rule whose whole input is a single labelled vertex can name what it \
creates after it.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c8e91f40-f7f5-754f-957e-56135aab792b"],

Cell["\<\
The shape of all this follows the reference paclet, so that rules written for \
that one read the same here, including the label-variable rules of its \
chemoid notebooks.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c5d9c053-9688-6749-b1a2-7731dbf293a4"],

Cell["Rewriting systems and causality", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"be9c7fd0-aaeb-5a4b-8e52-006d93f79b49"],

Cell["\<\
A rewriting system is rules together with a state to start from. Evolving it \
applies every rule in every way it fits, to every state reached so far, and \
what comes out is a tree of state occurrences joined by events.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"169c8f3d-3f68-9847-a182-e231bd948bd1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphRewritingSystem", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"56afe12f-049f-684d-b4cf-5c06440aba1b"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "rules and an initial state, with the evolution as properties"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c626cc36-6c40-ac4d-98f2-b058c60304a3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphRewritingSystemQ", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"a10e947e-abc6-6540-b144-00b8e2a26154"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "test for a valid system"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e08857f6-e6e2-c947-a65e-5cef65bb50af"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphCausalGraph", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"411e205c-ccd9-e643-95e7-576ec2f7f1ab"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the events, and which of them depended on which"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a3bcf6ea-5026-df4c-a89f-b39732bb21e0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["$CausalDependenceTypes", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"58f08774-716c-8e4a-b52d-e453d29ea121"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the readings of causal dependence on offer"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6451dfaf-6e5b-b849-aca9-2e51f996bfe4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["$HypergraphRewritingOptions", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"c327bbe2-d2bc-8746-a948-385395441e1c"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the registry of options, with their defaults"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fa864875-181d-2942-97f4-2f448181fff1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphRulePlot", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"13d92d12-1512-1640-b3a4-3b91de4a4715"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "a rule drawn: its input beside its output"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"42099408-7adf-4a4e-9d81-58323751ca4d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphEventPlot", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"8dadb12e-f259-9e48-9b56-d33a67fde8a3"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "an event drawn: the match highlighted in what was there, and the creations \
in what came of it"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"475a3771-bf7a-0247-8e09-ebae8814d910"],

Cell["\<\
The properties mirror what the reference paclets give: \"EvolutionGraph\" for \
the tree of state occurrences, \"StatesGraph\" for the same states merged, \
\"BranchialGraph\" for the states one step could have reached, and \
\"CausalGraph\" and \"EvolutionCausalGraph\" for the events and their \
dependence.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"50d4459a-11a7-9d4a-af60-fc8862eb06a1"],

Cell["\<\
What is not mirrored is that causal dependence here is a choice rather than a \
fixed meaning. Two events are related when the elements they touch overlap, \
and the option \"CausalDependence\" says what an element is: anything at all, \
vertex or edge, which is the weakest reading and the one the reference \
paclets take, where two rule applications are related as soon as their \
matched patterns are superposed; or whole edges only, which relates two \
events just when one consumed an edge the other made. The two readings differ \
on a real case \[LongDash] two compositions in disjoint parts of a chain \
share no arrow, but do share the object between them \[LongDash] and which is \
wanted is a fact about what the hypergraph stands for rather than about the \
rewriting.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"394fd45e-3d2f-704d-b675-1db100b3bdfe"],

Cell["\<\
Elements are followed by token rather than by value, since an edge is an \
element of a multiset and two edges that look the same are still two \
elements. A causal edge reports not only that two events are related but \
which elements they had in common.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"891ed445-8b1a-eb47-964c-29ea2eee4df0"],

Cell["\<\
A state is drawn in a graph as a framed picture of the hypergraph, and an \
event as the hypergraph it acted on with the match highlighted, an arrow, and \
what it made with the creations highlighted \[LongDash] the same two halves \
HypergraphEventPlot gives on its own. Both halves share a layout, so that \
what changed is what moves. The colours are those of the Wolfram Physics \
Project, which is what the reference paclets draw in, so that a graph made \
here reads the same way as one made there; the values are copied rather than \
fetched, since a package that cannot be loaded without a network is not worth \
the exactness.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"40331796-ea26-ca44-a12a-eca993824ae7"],

Cell["\<\
Drawing a state means laying out a hypergraph and drawing an event means \
laying out two, so past \"MaxDrawnVertices\" a graph falls back to plain \
vertices and says so. \"StateRendering\" and \"EventRendering\" force the \
question either way, and \"PanelSize\" sets how big each picture is.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9b19f83c-665b-af46-ba76-adbe1f96cee9"],

Cell["Not yet implemented", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3209acfc-c4fd-ee42-8fa2-e16a84fbd6e3"],

Cell["\<\
The objects, isomorphism, the array algebra, the drawing, the adjacency \
hypermatrix, rewriting and the causal machinery are all in place. What \
remains are the plex diagrams that tie rewriting to hypermatrix algebra, and \
a visual editor for hypergraphs and for rules.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"17e414d7-b1c2-c343-b954-38fbdf58f259"]
},
WindowSize->{820, 750},
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Microsoft Windows (64-bit) (July 2, 2026)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"2ded3ccc-7ea3-6846-a6c9-db2701d1865c"
]
